# PokeVault — Pokémon Card Portfolio Tracker

Track your Pokémon TCG collection in SGD with live pricing, P/L tracking, grade multipliers, and portfolio analytics.

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Backend | Node.js + Express 5 |
| Database | Supabase (PostgreSQL) |
| Auth | express-session + bcryptjs |
| Session store | connect-pg-simple (PostgreSQL) |
| Pricing API | PokéPrice.io |
| Frontend | Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS + Chart.js 4 |
| Hosting | Render (web service) |

---

## File Structure

```
pokevault/
├── server.js           # Express backend — all API routes
├── index.html          # Main collection page
├── stats.html          # Portfolio analytics page
├── login.html          # Login / register page
├── script.js           # Frontend logic for index.html
├── style.css           # Shared stylesheet (dark + light themes)
├── pfp.jpeg            # Brand logo / favicon
├── package.json        # Dependencies
├── .env.example        # Environment variable template
├── .gitignore
└── supabase_schema.sql # Run this once in Supabase SQL Editor
```

---

## Phase 1 — Supabase Setup (Database)

### Option A: Fresh Supabase project (recommended)

1. Go to [supabase.com](https://supabase.com) → **New project**
2. Choose a name (e.g. `pokevault`), set a strong database password, pick a region close to Singapore (e.g. Southeast Asia / Singapore)
3. Wait ~2 minutes for provisioning

### Run the schema

1. In your Supabase dashboard → **SQL Editor** → **New query**
2. Paste the entire contents of `supabase_schema.sql`
3. Click **Run** — you should see "Success. No rows returned"

### Collect your credentials

You need 3 values from Supabase:

| Value | Where to find it |
|---|---|
| `SUPABASE_URL` | Dashboard → Project Settings → API → **Project URL** |
| `SUPABASE_KEY` | Dashboard → Project Settings → API → **anon / public** key |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Dashboard → Project Settings → Database → **Connection string** → **URI** tab → choose **"Direct connection"** (port 5432) |

> ⚠️ **Critical:** For `DATABASE_URL`, use the **Direct connection** URI (port **5432**), NOT the Session Mode or Transaction Mode pooler (port 6543). The pooler URL format breaks `connect-pg-simple`.

The direct URI looks like:
```
postgresql://postgres:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@db.abcdefghijkl.supabase.co:5432/postgres
```

---

## Phase 2 — Render Deployment

### Create a new Web Service

1. Go to [render.com](https://render.com) → **New** → **Web Service**
2. Connect your GitHub repo containing this codebase
3. Configure:
   - **Name:** `pokevault` (or anything)
   - **Runtime:** Node
   - **Build command:** `npm install`
   - **Start command:** `npm start`
   - **Instance type:** Free (or paid for better performance)

### Set Environment Variables

In Render → your service → **Environment** → add these 5 variables:

| Variable | Value |
|---|---|
| `SUPABASE_URL` | Your Supabase project URL |
| `SUPABASE_KEY` | Your Supabase anon/public key |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Your Supabase direct connection URI (port 5432) |
| `POKEPRICE_KEY` | Your PokéPrice API key |
| `SESSION_SECRET` | Any random string, 32+ characters |

To generate a secure `SESSION_SECRET`, visit: https://generate-secret.vercel.app/32

### Deploy

Click **Deploy** (or it auto-deploys on git push). First deploy takes ~2 minutes.

---

## Phase 3 — Verification Checklist

After deploy, visit your Render URL and check:

- [ ] Login page loads at `/login.html`
- [ ] You can register a new account
- [ ] You can log in
- [ ] Main collection page loads (redirects from `/`)
- [ ] "Add card" form opens and card search works
- [ ] "↻ Refresh prices" fetches prices successfully
- [ ] Stats page at `/stats.html` loads charts

If you see a 500 error, check Render logs (Dashboard → your service → **Logs**). The most common cause is a missing or malformed `DATABASE_URL`.

---

## Local Development

```bash
# 1. Clone / copy files
# 2. Create .env from template
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your real values

# 3. Install dependencies
npm install

# 4. Run
npm start
# or with auto-restart:
npm run dev
```

App runs at http://localhost:5000

---

## Environment Variables Reference

| Variable | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `SUPABASE_URL` | ✅ | Supabase project URL |
| `SUPABASE_KEY` | ✅ | Supabase anon public key |
| `DATABASE_URL` | ✅ | PostgreSQL direct connection URI (port 5432) |
| `POKEPRICE_KEY` | ✅ | PokéPrice.io API key |
| `SESSION_SECRET` | ✅ | Secret for signing session cookies |
| `PORT` | auto | Render sets this automatically |

---

## Features

- **Multi-user** auth with hashed passwords (bcryptjs)
- **Card search** via PokéPrice API with visual picker
- **Live pricing** in SGD with USD/SGD FX conversion
- **Grade multipliers** (PSA 10: 3.5×, PSA 9: 1.5×, etc.)
- **Price history** charted per card
- **Target price alerts** — toast notification when market hits your target
- **Sold cards** tracking with realised P/L
- **CSV export** of full collection
- **Dark / light theme** with persistence
- **Mobile responsive** with card-list view on small screens
- **Newcomer tutorial** overlay
- **Stats page** — portfolio over time, type/grade breakdowns, ROI rankings
